    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Keller is a 79-year-old woman, deafblind since infancy, who called by text relay for a same-day visit. The history was taken through the clinic&apos;s on-call qualified tactile interpreter, who arrived 30 minutes after she did; she chose to wait rather than have her assistant interpret. For two days she has had burning on passing urine, frequency, and urgency, with no leakage. She has had no fever, chills, flank or back pain, nausea, vaginal discharge, or blood she could detect, and her assistant has noticed no change in her urine. She had one similar episode years ago that cleared with a short course of antibiotics. She has no allergies and takes no regular medicines. She is drinking well. She is due to travel to speak in ten days. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Bladder and urethra; no flank pain</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Two days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Burning on voiding with frequency and urgency</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; wakes twice a night to void</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>One similar episode years ago; trip in ten days</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Fluids help a little</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Denies fever, chills, flank pain, nausea, vaginal symptoms, and confusion</td></tr><tr><td>Communication</td><td>Qualified tactile interpreter; she chose to wait for one</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

